\tag{discrete}
\taxon{Example}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{“#{n} is odd.” ##{\Odd(n) = (\ext{k}{\Z} 2k + 1 = n).} Or we could define it as #{\neg \Even(n)}. (It is actually slightly nontrivial to prove formally that #{\Odd(n) \equiv \neg \Even(n)}—we won’t be able to prove it until we go over the Division Algorithm later in the semester!)}
